UID:hgse-20260826-2nd-edition-of-the-helsinki-economics-of-education-worksh
 op@helsinkigse.fi
DTSTAMP:20261113T054444Z
SEQUENCE:20
LAST-MODIFIED:20261113T054444Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Helsinki:20260826T090000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Helsinki:20260827T150000
SUMMARY:2nd Edition of the Helsinki Economics of Education Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Series: Economics of Education (Educa)\nType: Workshop\nTitle: 
 2nd Edition of the Helsinki Economics of Education Workshop\nHost: Cécile
  Bonneau\n\nProgramme:\n\nWednesday 26 August\n\n09:00–09:25 Welcome and
  morning coffee\n\n09:25–09:30 Welcome word\n\n09:30–10:30\n• Mikkel
  Houmark — Teachers and Inequality in Student Performance – Estimating
  Value Added and Sorting under Endogenous Mobility\, with Mathias Mørk\n
 • Ossi Tahvonen — Cash Transfers\, Health\, and the Transition to Adul
 thood\n\n10:30–11:00 Coffee break\n\n11:00–12:00\n• Gregory Veramend
 i — Smartphones and Childrens' Mental Health\n• Shushanik Margaryan 
 — Affirmative Action during Early Childhood: School Choice\, Academic Pe
 rformance and School Satisfaction\, with José Montalbán\n\n12:00–13:30
  Lunch in Arvo Restaurant\n\n13:30–14:30\n• Camille Terrier — Foster
 ing Social Integration in the Classroom: Evidence from a Peer-Learning Exp
 eriment\, with Rustam Hakimov and Fanny Landaud\n• Libertad Gonzalez —
  Born Too Soon? The Educational Costs of Early Elective Deliveries\, with 
 Parijat Maitra\n\n14:45–15:45\n• Aino Kalmbach — Priority Pitfalls: 
 Admission Mechanisms and Educational Outcomes\n• Rasmus Mellanen — Pee
 r Effects on Educational Choices: Evidence from Finnish Weighted Curriculu
 m Classes\n• Moritz Mendel — Expectation Formation and Educational Inv
 estment: Evidence from Labor Market Shocks\, with Alex Armand\, Pedro Carn
 eiro\, and Alessandro Toppeta\n• Théophile Mulot — The Role of Parent
 al Role Models in the Gendered Choice of STEM Studies\, with Cécile Bonne
 au\n• Lachlan Paterson — The Role of Training Providers in Immigrant I
 ntegration\, with Hanna Pesola and Tuomo Virkola\n• Arkādijs Zvaigzne 
 — Success Begets Success: The Dynamic Treatment Effects of Financial Aid
  Tournaments\n\n16:00–17:00\n• Matti Sarvimäki — Learning to Experi
 ment: Field Experiments in Finnish Education\n• Anna Holvio — Reading 
 Gains Through Teacher Pairs: A Co-Teaching Experiment\, with Hannu Karhune
 n\, Marja-Kristiina Lerkkanen\, Matti Sarvimäki\, and Minna Torppa\n• M
 ikko Silliman — Building a Shared Reality: Social Cohesion in Diverse Cl
 assrooms\, Michela Carlana\, Ellen Sahlström\, Matti Sarvimäki\, and Mar
 co Tabellini\n• Maria Sauval — Finding One’s Path: Career-Counselor 
 Training and Students’ Educational Choices\, with Hanna Pesola and Matti
  Sarvimäki\n• Ramin Izadi — Reforming Universal Early Childhood Educa
 tion: Finland’s Two-Year Preschool Experiment\, with Oskari Harjunen\, A
 nna Holvio and Matti Sarvimäki\n\n19:00\nWorkshop Dinner for presenters a
 t Yes Yes Yes\n\nThursday 27 August\n\n09:00–09:30 Welcome and morning c
 offee\n\n09:30–10:30\n• Lavinia Kinne — Diversity in Teams and Creat
 ive Output\, with Raphael Brade and Margaret Leighton\n• Ellen Sahlströ
 m — The Broad Effects of Providing Long-Term Support to Disadvantaged Bo
 ys\n\n10:30–11:00 Coffee break\n\n11:00–12:00\nKeynote — Kirabo Jack
 son « The Returns to Public Investment in Children »\n\n12:00–13:30 Lu
 nch in Arvo Restaurant\n\n13:30–14:30\n• Aspasia Bizopoulou — Fast T
 ransit and Human Capital Accumulation\, with Nektarios Aslanidis and Sande
 r Ramboer\n• Miika Päällysaho — Decomposing Trends in the PISA Study
 \, with Jani Kuhakoski and Roope Uusitalo\n• Cécile Bonneau — Price o
 f Admission: The Impact of Application Fees on Top Students\n• Hanna Vir
 tanen — Information Alone Is Not Enough: Randomized Trials of Lifelong L
 earning Interventions for Low-Educated Adults\, with Antti Kauhanen\, Hann
 u Karhunen\, Jani Kuhakoski\, Krista Riukula\, and Tuomo Suhonen\n\n14:30
 –15:00 Coffee break\n\n15:00 End of workshop\n\nTimes read from the prog
 ramme.\n\nFull programme: https://www.helsinkigse.fi/media/pages/events/2n
 d-edition-of-the-helsinki-economics-of-education-workshop/41ca027d73-17877
 21315/heew_workshop__2026.pdf\nEvent page: https://www.helsinkigse.fi/even
 ts/2nd-edition-of-the-helsinki-economics-of-education-workshop
LOCATION:V001\, Aalto University School of Business\, Ekonominaukio 1\, Esp
 oo
URL:https://www.helsinkigse.fi/events/2nd-edition-of-the-helsinki-economics
 -of-education-workshop
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
